1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Now let's take a look at how to use the animation character in M.I.E. to create a costume animation.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:23,000
First, in M.I.E. prepare the joint key needle.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Then select the body grid for the Alambic file.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:37,000
You can also use other formats, such as FBX and PC2, but in this video, we will show you how to use Alambic.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000
After selecting the body, save the animation file.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Open the costume file in Marvelous Designer.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Then import the Alambic file that you saved from M.I.E.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Then adjust the surface of the model.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The surface diameter determines the distance between the body grid and the costume in the simulation process.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Since the character we use in this video is much smaller than the normal adult, we will reduce the surface diameter to default.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Activate the simulation or press the control key to check if the costume is correctly worn on the body.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
After pausing the simulation, click the record button to start the animation operation and record the animation at the same time.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,000
After the animation is completed, the costume with the animation will be exported to M.I.E.

14
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,000
I will export the costume animation to the Alambic file, which is the most commonly used file type.

15
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
But please note that you can also use other formats, such as PCO and MC.

16
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
For example, if you need to merge the connection point, please select the merge option.

17
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
In addition, please select the unified UV coordinates.

18
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,000
To export the UV created by you in Marvelous Designer.

19
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,000
If you don't need to prepare the pattern, you can cancel it in the following options box.

20
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:13,000
I will choose 0mm as the unit in the ratio because it is the same unit as we used when exporting.

21
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Then select the confirm button.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Now let's import the costume file to M.I.E.

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
You can press cache to save.

24
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Alambic cache Alambic to save.

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Go to Alambic to find and select the costume file.

26
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Now you can start animation costumes and work in M.I.E.

